# Regression for a related bug found alongside the parse_if overflow
# above: compile_definition's outer_known_types/outer_known_type_sets
# save/restore around a nested def used to copy a fixed 256 elements
# instead of outer_next_register-many, so entries [256, outer_next_
# register) were silently left holding whatever the nested def's own
# (unrelated) body wrote into those same register indices, rather than
# being restored to the enclosing scope's own values.
